                <pb facs="0563" n="451" sameAs="frus:frus1935v03/pg451"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.01 Outer Mongolia/41: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Counselor of Embassy in China</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Lockhart</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-11-27T18:00:00+08:00">November 27, 1935—6
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received November 27—8:55 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>183. Following telegram has been received from the Consul General at Harbin.</p>
                <quote rend="blockquote">
                    <p>“52. November 27, noon. The Japanese Consulate General has confirmed press
                        reports that the Manchuli conference has broken down and that the delegates
                        are leaving. Apparently no agreement of any nature was reached. In a
                        statement the Hsinking Foreign Office laid the responsibility for failure on
                        Outer Mongolia and found ‘no alternative but to act freely in the
                        future’.”</p>
                </quote>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lockhart</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
